**Date:** 28 October 2026 · **Replaces:** [0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) · **Deciders:** support desk

## Context

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports whose subject lines match.
[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) shows what that costs: three problems arrive under the same subject
lines, so all of them were merged into one ticket, marked known, and given one fix. The fix
covered one of the three ([#4472](/kb/incidents/4472)).

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} repo="https://github.com/AdditionAddict/support-kb-4471" tickets={{ parser: 1, hint: 2, 'one-day': 3 }} />

## Decision

Two reports are the same issue when they have the **same cause**, not the same subject:

1. look up the reporter's tenant: its locale and its booking form (`causes.ts`, `sameCause`);
2. never use intake's tag: it is a guess from the reporter's browser;
3. a report the desk reads differently from its tenant's cause (`desk-notes.json`) gets its own
   ticket, not a footnote under another one.

No cause on file: keep the report apart until someone reads it.

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## Consequences

- Triage needs a tenant lookup instead of a glance at the subject. The lookup is code that
  already runs on every build.
- A ticket's count means one problem. A fix closes the ticket it fixes, not its neighbours.
- 0001 stays as written; this record replaces it once accepted.

